@*
    What it can do.

    MARKETING. NOT SETTINGS.

    This screen used to have "Turn on" buttons, a tab of free space and memory
    readings, and a technical details panel - a download manager and a diagnostics
    page wearing the name of a promise. Configuration belongs in Settings, where
    somebody goes when they want to change something; this screen exists for the
    moment before that, when they are deciding whether the thing is worth having
    at all.

    So there are no controls. Nothing to turn on, nothing to measure, nothing that
    can be got wrong. It says what the phone will do for you and shows you where
    to start.

    NOTHING SCROLLS: four claims and a way in.
*@
@page "/abilities"
@inject IFormFactor Host

<div class="pitch">

    <h1 class="lead">It does the things you would ask a person</h1>

    <div class="claims">
        <div class="claim">
            <span class="claim-icon" aria-hidden="true">🗣</span>
            <span class="claim-text">
                <span class="claim-title">It talks, in your language</span>
                <span class="claim-sub">75 languages, spoken out loud - including the ones
                    the big assistants never learned.</span>
            </span>
        </div>

        @*
            THE OFFLINE PROMISE IS ONLY PRINTED WHERE IT IS TRUE. In a browser tab
            the models are not there, and marketing that lies is worse than
            marketing that says less.
        *@
        @if (Host.IsOnDevice)
        {
            <div class="claim">
                <span class="claim-icon" aria-hidden="true">📵</span>
                <span class="claim-text">
                    <span class="claim-title">It works with no signal</span>
                    <span class="claim-sub">Everything runs on this phone. No data, no
                        waiting for a tower.</span>
                </span>
            </div>
        }

        <div class="claim">
            <span class="claim-icon" aria-hidden="true">🔒</span>
            <span class="claim-text">
                <span class="claim-title">It keeps what it knows</span>
                <span class="claim-sub">Your CV, your details, your conversations - here,
                    not on somebody else's computer.</span>
            </span>
        </div>

        <div class="claim">
            <span class="claim-icon" aria-hidden="true">🆓</span>
            <span class="claim-text">
                <span class="claim-title">It costs nothing</span>
                <span class="claim-sub">No account, no subscription. Only a search you asked
                    for ever leaves the phone.</span>
            </span>
        </div>
    </div>

    <a class="start" href="services">See everything it helps with</a>

</div>


